{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 2a803a6966bc01f989710049bfd83a64863b0951 on builder/ar5-activation-marker-20261117, all 7 artifacts, for request 9a71d76b under my promise 4ec221f6. The implementation is AR-5 (request 28d62918, promise b5ba9d28, ruling 261e9b3e). The reporting artifact is the AR-5 note. The head's parent is main 957e0ba4.\n\nMy AR-4 approval (a4a71300) said that only Directory commits drop the Directory's marker. I took that from the docstring and did not list the callers of `committed()`. The constructor's activation was one of them. For this head I listed every caller that writes the archive wake.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole source diff.\n- `archive-row.ts`. `signal(at, budget, sealed = true)` now returns early on a `\"directory\"` marker when `sealed` is false. A `\"member\"` marker stays for every call, as in AR-4. A sealed call on a Directory marker still writes `next: at`.\n- `archive-driver.ts`. `committed(sealed = true)` passes `sealed` to `signal()`.\n- `object.ts`. The constructor's activation calls `committed(false)`. The `onSealed` hook (`object.ts:320-324`) keeps `committed()`, which means sealed.\n- The seal moves for `ScopeObject`, `archive-driver.ts` and `archive-row.ts` name AR-5.\n\nEvery writer of the archive wake at this head:\n\n- `onSealed` → `committed()` → `signal(sealed)`: one write per sealed entry. On a Directory marker it wakes the Directory at once. On a member marker it does nothing.\n- Activation → `committed(false)` → `signal(not sealed)`: leaves both markers. Without a marker it still writes `next: now` when no wake is due, as before AR-4.\n- The pass: `defer()` (pre-Mark retry, AR-1 backoff), `unbound()` (marker, one day), `clearWake()` (idle), and `#retryWake()` (persists a backed-off wake after an early return).\n- `restart()` is an operator command for a stopped `limit` or `foreign-source-unavailable` row. It does not touch markers.\n- Every alarm calls `archive.run()` (`object.ts:996`). While the stored wake is in the future, the wake check at `archive-driver.ts:218-219` ends that pass before any port call.\n\nWake rate (rule review-wake-rate-of-background-work):\n\n- The floor between passes for an unbound scope is one day. A construction makes no pass, so an object that the platform evicts and builds again each minute no longer sets the floor. A sealed Directory commit wakes the Directory sooner. That is the binding path the ruling wants.\n- What stops a reschedule loop: the same as AR-4. A due recheck makes one pass, which stores the marker again for a day or takes the AR-1 backoff.\n- grow-demo, requests per hour. Before AR-4: about 98 (AR-3). With AR-4: about 360, from the Directory's pass each minute (rate read cd9b8e19). After AR-5: about 4 expected. That is four rechecks a day at about 24 requests each, from AR-3's 98 an hour for four hourly passes. The note's \"under 1\" undercounts the requests per recheck. The ruling's \"~4\" is the right figure. The Membership pin pass each minute is separate and unchanged.\n- One condition holds this figure: the Directory must not seal an entry each minute. The note's minute log shows only reads into the Directory (`nativeBirth`, `archiveItem`). The deployment rate read confirms it: if the Directory still makes a pass each minute, a sealed commit is the cause.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The red. `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-ar5-red/red.txt` runs the two new cases without the source change: 2 fail and 21 pass, with \"an activation leaves the Directory's marker\".\n- The gate. Run 3 (END 552e3927) passed at this head: plain 4,998 and native 1,194. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\". Runs 1 and 2 failed on single plain-stage timeouts in derive and git under outside load. Neither run reached the native stage, and AR-5 touches neither package.\n- Scope. The 7 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 957e0ba4 2a803a69`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The fix names the difference that AR-4 missed: a sealed entry against a construction. The default `sealed = true` keeps every other caller's behavior, and the one call that changes is the activation.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The head narrows when a wake is written and adds no port, route or reader. A stopped writer stays stopped.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The rate table in the note says \"under 1\" for AR-5. A later note can correct it to about 4.\n\nFacts for the planner's deployment: deploy the room Workers and read the DO rate on dap-grow. Expect the Directory to make no pass after its first activation under AR-5, and the hourly rate to fall to the pre-AR-4 floor minus the old :35 burst.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0587b40c86490656a84ee2d8474745c068c2f839","binding":"assigned","head":"2a803a6966bc01f989710049bfd83a64863b0951","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4ec221f6f756cd091db46eff29fcad760ebce758\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5ba9d283945a99094633aad314167941c0362cf\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4ec221f6f756cd091db46eff29fcad760ebce758","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}